{"id":"e05t3","name":"First Overdraft per Account","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A bank wants to know when each account went into overdraft for the first time. You have two tables.</p>\n<p><b>accounts</b>: <code>account_id</code> and <code>opening_balance</code> (numeric).</p>\n<p><b>movements</b>: <code>movement_id</code> (integer, unique), <code>account_id</code>, <code>booked_at</code> (timestamp) and <code>amount</code> (numeric, positive for a deposit, negative for a withdrawal). Movements are applied in order of <code>booked_at</code>, then <code>movement_id</code> when two movements have the same time.</p>\n<p>The balance after a movement is the opening balance plus the sum of all movements of the account up to this one, included.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return, for every account whose balance becomes <b>strictly negative</b> at least once, the first movement that made it negative, with the columns <code>account_id</code>, <code>movement_id</code>, <code>booked_at</code> and <code>balance</code> (the balance after this movement), sorted by <code>account_id</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>accounts</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>account_id</th><th>opening_balance</th></tr><tr><td>A1</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>A2</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>A3</td><td>50</td></tr></table></div><p>Table <code>movements</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>movement_id</th><th>account_id</th><th>booked_at</th><th>amount</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>A1</td><td>2026-03-01 09:00:00</td><td>-60</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>A1</td><td>2026-03-01 10:00:00</td><td>-50</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>A1</td><td>2026-03-02 10:00:00</td><td>200</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>A1</td><td>2026-03-03 10:00:00</td><td>-400</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>A2</td><td>2026-03-01 08:00:00</td><td>30</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>A2</td><td>2026-03-01 12:00:00</td><td>-30</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>A2</td><td>2026-03-01 12:00:00</td><td>-10</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>A3</td><td>2026-03-04 08:00:00</td><td>-50</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>account_id</th><th>movement_id</th><th>booked_at</th><th>balance</th></tr><tr><td>A1</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-01 10:00:00</td><td>-10.0</td></tr><tr><td>A2</td><td>7</td><td>2026-03-01 12:00:00</td><td>-10.0</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>accounts</code>, <code>movements</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>account_id</code>, <code>movement_id</code>, <code>booked_at</code>, <code>balance</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["somme cumulée","SUM OVER ORDER BY","départage par id","première occurrence"],"minutes":15,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>accounts</code>, <code>movements</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 4 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>account_id</code>, <code>movement_id</code>, <code>booked_at</code>, <code>balance</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; les dates s'affichent AAAA-MM-JJ HH:MM:SS pour une date avec heure.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 7 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"accounts":{"columns":[["account_id","VARCHAR(5)"],["opening_balance","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[["A1",100],["A2",0],["A3",50]]},"movements":{"columns":[["movement_id","INT"],["account_id","VARCHAR(5)"],["booked_at","TIMESTAMP"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[[1,"A1","2026-03-01 09:00:00",-60],[2,"A1","2026-03-01 10:00:00",-50],[3,"A1","2026-03-02 10:00:00",200],[4,"A1","2026-03-03 10:00:00",-400],[5,"A2","2026-03-01 08:00:00",30],[7,"A2","2026-03-01 12:00:00",-30],[6,"A2","2026-03-01 12:00:00",-10],[8,"A3","2026-03-04 08:00:00",-50]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["account_id","movement_id","booked_at","balance"],"rows":[["A1",2,"2026-03-01 10:00:00",-10.0],["A2",7,"2026-03-01 12:00:00",-10.0]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"accounts":{"columns":[["account_id","VARCHAR(5)"],["opening_balance","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[["Z",10]]},"movements":{"columns":[["movement_id","INT"],["account_id","VARCHAR(5)"],["booked_at","TIMESTAMP"],["amount","NUMERIC(10,2)"]],"rows":[[2,"Z","2026-01-01 00:00:00",5],[1,"Z","2026-01-01 00:00:00",-12]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["account_id","movement_id","booked_at","balance"],"rows":[["Z",1,"2026-01-01 00:00:00",-2.0]]}}],"hidden_n":7,"hidden":"","solution":""}